WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.360
What can three families show that no screen in a dish could?

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:11.170
Pain signals start in sensory neurons called nociceptors.

3
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.550
Their spikes need voltage-gated sodium channels.

4
00:00:15.583 --> 00:00:19.343
The channel in this story was not nominated by a screen in a dish.

5
00:00:20.123 --> 00:00:21.303
It was found in families.

6
00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:27.173
Three consanguineous families in northern Pakistan had members who had never

7
00:00:27.173 --> 00:00:28.253
experienced pain.

8
00:00:29.317 --> 00:00:32.237
Six affected children were examined clinically.

9
00:00:33.157 --> 00:00:34.537
They were aged 4 to 14.

10
00:00:35.617 --> 00:00:37.517
The condition was recessive.

11
00:00:38.297 --> 00:00:41.217
Affected children carried two broken copies of one gene.

12
00:00:42.217 --> 00:00:48.657
Mapping and sequencing found three different homozygous nonsense mutations in SCN9A.

13
00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:55.790
That gene encodes Nav1.7, a sodium channel concentrated in pain-sensing neurons.

14
00:00:56.883 --> 00:00:58.983
A gene now travels with the phenotype.

15
00:00:59.943 --> 00:01:01.623
What measurement would you insist on next?

16
00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.447
Linkage says the variant travels with the phenotype.

17
00:01:11.407 --> 00:01:13.247
It cannot say the protein stopped working.

18
00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:18.687
A nonsense allele is not by itself proof of absent functional current.

19
00:01:19.527 --> 00:01:25.487
Expressing mutant cDNA tests the construct's functional output, without reproducing

20
00:01:25.487 --> 00:01:30.027
native transcript processing or measuring protein abundance in a patient's neurons.

21
00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:34.600
So put the mutant channel in cultured cells and look for current.

22
00:01:35.583 --> 00:01:39.403
The mutant constructs gave no current above the recording background.

23
00:01:40.143 --> 00:01:44.123
That is no measurable conduction, not a proven absence of protein.

24
00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:48.327
So the genetics and the biophysics pointed the same way.

25
00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:53.747
Lose this one channel, and the painful world goes quiet while touch continues.

26
00:01:54.817 --> 00:01:59.597
The children could still tell hot food from cold, though temperature sensation was

27
00:01:59.597 --> 00:02:00.777
not rigorously assessed.

28
00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.890
The loss is not confined to pain.

29
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:07.610
People with the same loss of function also cannot smell.

30
00:02:08.633 --> 00:02:13.433
That result turned the channel into a major target for analgesic drug development.

31
00:02:14.517 --> 00:02:16.017
It also set a standard.

32
00:02:16.857 --> 00:02:20.177
A human pain gene should arrive with a channel measurement attached.

33
00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:25.390
Human genetics supplied both the gene and the direction of its effect.

34
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.460
Here is the puzzle this lesson answers.

35
00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:32.120
The blocker that reached patients blocks a different channel.

36
00:02:33.083 --> 00:02:34.503
Hold that gap in mind.

37
00:02:35.743 --> 00:02:39.043
Genetics nominated one channel, and the drug that worked blocks another.

38
00:02:40.117 --> 00:02:42.357
Human genetics can nominate a channel.

39
00:02:43.297 --> 00:02:45.817
Only a recording can say whether the channel conducts.
